  "extras": [],
  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What communication is legal for Tali’s Silver (Commune with Spirits)?",
      "answer": "All Table Talk and Communication is fully open - to teammates and opponents (p. 4). A Tali player can give teammates instructions like “Say Blue” or “Say Red if Sabina plays Gold, otherwise say Green,” as long as the opponents can hear (and understand) these instructions. The Tali player may not secretly indicate their desire to their teammates by whispering, gestures, showing cards, a private code, etc.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "If Tali tries to resolve her Silver (Commune with Spirits) and her whole team is dead or immune, what happens?",
      "answer": "No friendly hero can be chosen and the card does nothing.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    },
    {
      "question": "Tali’s Alternate Green (Ancestral Totem) makes a Totem that can protect a minion. If the Totem is removed, does the Hero gain coins?",
      "answer": "No. The Totem is removed instead of the minion being defeated, so no minion is defeated and no coins are gained.",
      "source": "goa2-faq"
    }
  ],
  "lore": "When she heard their voices for the first time, no one believed her. Tali held no grudges. When the frost beasts threatened her tribe, she did what she had to do. And when the village was saved, she left — the spirits were calling her.",
